---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why GuestGuideIQ exists: hyperlocal travel knowledge, built into the guest guides people already open."
>
  <section class="wrap section about-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why we're building this</span>
    <h1>Every place has an Alfama bakery. Most travelers never find it.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The internet made it easier than ever to find the ten most-photographed things to do in
      any city — and, somehow, harder to find what the people who live there actually do. Every
      "hidden gem" list reads the same because it's built the same way: scraped, ranked, and
      repeated across a thousand sites.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section-tight about-body">
    <p>
      GuestGuideIQ starts from a different question: not "what ranks well," but "what does a
      local actually tell a friend who's visiting?" That knowledge exists — it just doesn't live
      anywhere a traveler can find it before they've already left.
    </p>
    <p>
      Short-term rentals turned out to be the right place to put it. A host already has a
      relationship with their guest, and guests already open a property guide to find the wifi
      password and check-out time. That's a real, trusted moment to put hyperlocal knowledge in
      front of someone — without asking them to discover, download, and trust a whole new app
      first.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our vision is simple: every stay comes with a local's know-how built in, and every local
      business or guide gets a real chance to be discovered by the people already standing in
      their neighborhood.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section-tight about-contact">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Investors &amp; press</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Want the fuller story, our roadmap, or just to ask a question? Reach out through{' '}
        <a href="/contact/">our contact page</a> — we read every message ourselves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .about-body {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .about-contact .card {
    padding: clamp(26px, 4vw, 36px);
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .about-contact h2 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
